# The Long Table. Homely, attentive, a little too interested in you. Nothing is ever described.
# No regard, no threats; the family's memory stays its three words (guest, family, crossed).

conv table.road.host
for table:road
topic "What's the road like ahead?"
prio world
voice table

node start
  say Clear as far as the bridge, if you keep off the verges. The trucks went through this morning, both of them, and nothing's come along behind them that I've seen.
  say Where are you headed, then? And is anyone expecting you back tonight?
  > @alone Nobody's expecting me. I'm on my own. -> alone
  > @expected They're expecting me back by dark. -> expected
  > @road I'm just passing through. -> passing

node alone
  say Then you'll eat with us tonight. Father cooks for twenty and there are never twenty any more. Supper's at half six, at the farmhouse up the lane, with the lamp in the window.
  do claim:alone
  > @maybe Maybe I will. Thank you. -> hub
  > @no Another time, maybe. -> hub

node expected
  say Then you'd best be on your way before the light goes. People worry when someone's late, these days. Come another day, and bring them with you. There's always room.
  do claim:expected; test:expected:20.5:300
  > @thanks Thanks. I'll mind the verges. -> hub

node passing
  say Everyone is, these days. That's what roads are for. The offer stands whenever you're passing next. Supper's at half six, and Father always asks after the ones who said no.
  > @back1 I'll remember that. -> hub

conv table.mother.house
for table:mother
when !table:crossed
topic "This is a big farm. Is it yours?"
prio flavour
voice table

node start
  say It was my husband's people's, three generations of them. Always a big house, always a long table, and always somebody at it. Sit, sit, love. You're thin as a rail.
  say Have you been bitten, love? We ask everyone who comes in. You can tell me. It doesn't change your welcome. Only how long you stay.
  > @no No. I haven't been bitten. -> fine
  > @bite I have. Here, look. -> bitten   if bite_shown
  > @boy Is that boy yours? -> boy

node fine
  say Good. Then there's no hurry at all, is there? Stay as long as you like. The roads will still be there in the morning, and so will we.
  > @back1 Thank you. Can I ask something else? -> hub

node bitten
  say Oh, love. I'm so sorry. Then you'll eat first, and we'll say a kind word over you, and you'll be on the road before dark. We learned that the hard way, back at the start.
  do call:slot:2
  > @back2 Thank you. Can I ask something else? -> hub

node boy
  say He came to us with the others, back at the start, when the houses sent us the ones they couldn't feed. He's ours now. He eats what he's given and never complains.
  > @back3 I see. Something else, then. -> hub

# The host on the road speaks first (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Who opens a conversation"): at 12 m, once a
# life, inside the unasked-contact budget. Nothing is ever described. Its line is a say? (the hub opens
# on the replies, so a plain line isn't shown): the first meeting, who he is and the question.
conv table.road.hello
for table:road
when !table:crossed
greet
opens approach 12
prio quest
once
voice table

node start
  say? !met :: Hello there. I'm from the farm up the lane, out walking the road with a flask like most days. You look done in. Where've you come from, and where are you off to?

# A claim the family tests (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Lies you're told"): "They're expecting me back by
# dark" is checked at 20:30. Still within 300 m of the road it was said on, it wasn't true.
conv table.road.still_expected
for table:road
when nmem:expected.false & !table:crossed
greet
prio reaction
once
voice table

node start
  say? nmem:expected.false :: Still expected, are you? It's gone half eight and here you are on the same road. Never mind, love. Supper was at half six, but there's always room.
